<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    "Your bird" (widgets phase 3): one cell (so it fits anywhere) up to two cells wide, where there is
    room for the mood and the step count beside the bird. Cell sizes follow the launcher formula
    (70dp * n - 30dp): 1 cell = 40dp, 2 cells = 110dp.

    updatePeriodMillis is 0 on purpose: Android's own periodic update is at most every 30 minutes and
    wakes the device for it. The refresh is BirdRefreshWorker's unique periodic work (30 min), plus the
    gateway's silent "crow-widgets" push and onUpdate.

    widgetCategory is home_screen only, never keyguard — the SAME rule as "What needs me": a widget that
    can sit on the lock screen has to reason about what a locked phone may show, and this one shows a
    step count. The provider still drops the step count for any host that places it there anyway (see
    BirdWidgetProvider.build, which reuses NeedsMeWidgetProvider.drawsOnKeyguard).
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/widget_bird"
    android:minWidth="40dp"
    android:minHeight="40dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="40dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="40dp"
    android:maxResizeWidth="110dp"
    android:maxResizeHeight="40dp"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen" />